const f=JSON.parse(`[{"id":"wordform-0","chapter":"wordform","title":"前缀（猜词义、写反义词）","md":"- ⭐ 变否定的形容词前缀：un-（unambitious, unsatisfied）、in-（inaccurate）、im-（immortal 不会死的，impolite）、il-（illiterate 不识字的）、ir-（irreplaceable 无法替代的，irrelevant 不相关的）、dis-（dissimilar 不一样的，dissatisfied）、a-（asymmetrical 不对称的，apolitical 不关心政治的）、un-（unconscious 失去知觉的）\\n  - Coral reefs are irreplaceable. Once they are destroyed, they are gone for ever.\\n  - Some students find history irrelevant to the modern world.\\n- ⭐ 别的常见前缀：mis-（错，misspelt 拼错的）、under-（不够，underfunded 资金不足的）、de-（去掉，denationalized 不再国有的）、over-（过度，overfishing 过度捕鱼）、re-（再，resit 重考）、out-（比……更久或更多，outlive 比……活得久）"},{"id":"wordform-1","chapter":"wordform","title":"后缀（变词性）","md":"- ⭐ 动词变名词：-ment（fulfil → fulfilment）、-ion（act → action，detect → detection）、-ation、-ing（travel → travelling）\\n- ⭐ 形容词变名词：-ness（sad → sadness，thoughtless → thoughtlessness）、-ity（rapid → rapidity，similar → similarity）\\n- ⭐ -hood、-ship 变名词：adulthood, childhood, neighbourhood；courtship, friendship, kingship, relationship\\n- ⭐ 变形容词：-ful（useful, wonderful）、-less（useless, worthless, priceless 无价的）、-al（survival 是名词，denial 是名词）、-ous（courageous）\\n  - Courageous people are not afraid of danger.\\n  - This old painting is priceless."},{"id":"wordform-2","chapter":"wordform","title":"评价动词三组（读作者态度用）","md":"- ⭐ 评估：assess, appraise, judge → 名词 assessment, appraisal, judgement\\n- ⭐ 赞同：endorse, condone（容忍）, appreciate, approve → endorsement, appreciation, approval\\n- ⭐ 反对：condemn, disapprove, censure, criticize → condemnation, disapproval, censure, criticism\\n- ⭐ 别的动词变名词：perceive → perception，believe → belief，think → thought，analyse → analysis，conceive → conception，discriminate → discrimination\\n  - The team carried out a detailed assessment of the risks involved.\\n  - Public condemnation of the use of money was very harsh.\\n- ⭐ 反义动词：defend ↔ oppose，undervalue ↔ overvalue，understand ↔ misunderstand，approve of ↔ disapprove of，praise ↔ criticize，judge ↔ misjudge，believe ↔ doubt"},{"id":"wordform-3","chapter":"wordform","title":"分类和特征的词","md":"- ⭐ 「特征」的同义词：feature = characteristic = trait = attribute = quality\\n- ⭐ 「种类」的说法：a make of car（车的牌子）、a species of animal、a genre of writing、a class of medicine、a field of study、a branch of medicine、a breed of horse、a strain of virus；通用的 type, sort, variety, brand\\n- ⭐ 词性变化：character → characterize → characteristic；distinction → distinguish → distinctive；example → exemplify；feature → feature；illustration → illustrate → illustrative；indication → indicate → indicative；type → typify → typical\\n- ⭐ 分类动词：classify, differentiate, define, catalogue, relate, satisfy (criteria)\\n  - Fungi may be classified into three broad groups.\\n  - Chimpanzees, gorillas and orangutans are all closely related species.\\n\\n\\n---"},{"id":"terms-0","chapter":"terms","title":"术语表","md":"| 术语 | 意思 | 备注 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| paraphrase | 换个说法改写 |  |\\n| illustrate / show / depict | 展示，说明（写图表开头用） |  |\\n| overview | 概述 |  |\\n| stage / step | 阶段 / 步骤 |  |\\n| cause / effect / consequence | 原因 / 影响 / 后果 |  |\\n| advantages / drawbacks / benefits | 优点 / 缺点 / 好处 |  |\\n| measures / solutions / steps | 措施 / 解决办法 / 步骤 |  |\\n| topic sentence | 主题句 |  |\\n| thesis statement | 立场句，中心论点 |  |\\n| body paragraph | 主体段 |  |\\n| conclusion | 结论 |  |\\n| keyword | 关键词 |  |\\n| Not Given | 文中没提到 |  |\\n| notes completion | 笔记填空 |  |\\n| homework (HW) | 作业 |  |\\n| English only | 只能说英语 |  |\\n\\n---"},{"id":"grammar-0","chapter":"grammar","title":"1. 时态","md":"- **一般现在时第三人称单数**：The illustration show**s**…（主语单数，动词加 s）\\n- **现在完成时**：I've known him for about 10 years, ever since we were classmates. / Many wells **have fallen** into disuse.（过去发生、影响到现在；for 加一段时间，since 加起点）\\n\\n- **将来时预测**（预测图必用）：\\n  - will + 动词原形：The number of solar-powered buildings will increase to 500 million in 2025.\\n  - It is predicted / projected / anticipated / forecast that… will…\\n  - The number is expected / set / forecast to increase to 500 million.\\n  - The prediction is that…\\n  - will have + 过去分词（某个将来时间点前已经完成）：By 2025, 500 million buildings will have converted to solar power.\\n  - will be + -ing（将来某时正在进行）：In 2025, 500 million buildings will be using solar power.\\n- **过去完成时 had done**：某个过去时间点之前已经完成的变化：By 2005, the block of flats had been turned into a hotel.（被动）/ had made way for a hotel.（主动）"},{"id":"grammar-1","chapter":"grammar","title":"2. 被动语态（流程图、历史描写必用）","md":"- 结构：is/are/was/were + 过去分词\\n- The beans are dried. They are then roasted. / It **was built** by Queen Udayamati.\\n- 主动改被动来改写句子：Many companies prefer experienced candidates. → Experienced candidates are preferred by many companies.\\n- 情态动词加被动：The number of working hours **should be reduced**.\\n- **自然过程用主动，人工生产用被动**：A river flows from its source to the ocean. / Many electronic goods are manufactured in Japan.\\n- **不及物动词不能变被动**：fall, rise, die, become 后面不接宾语，没有被动（The temperature falls.）\\n  - 只能及物：design, produce, send, manufacture, obtain\\n  - 两种都可以：begin, dry, grow, cool（Sunlight opens the leaves. / The leaves open.）\\n- **描写过去形成的过程用过去时被动**：Coal was formed over millions of years. The dead plants were covered by rocks and dirt. Coal is now mined.\\n- **流程句主谓一致**：The sun shines and the temperature rises."},{"id":"grammar-2","chapter":"grammar","title":"3. 名词和数量","md":"- 讲人数、数量用 number 或 quantity，quality 是质量：a remarkable decrease in **the number of** students\\n- **the number of + 单数动词**，**a number of + 复数动词**：The number of cars is rising. / A number of people are…\\n- many + 复数名词：many characteristics\\n- 可数名词用 fewer，不可数用 less\\n\\n- **不可数名词**：information, knowledge, research, weather, accommodation, nature, climate, progress, evidence, work, advice, equipment（不能加 s，不能用 a）；可数：animal, tree, idea, situation, fact\\n  - 把可数换成不可数时动词也要改：These facts are… → This information is…\\n- **冠词**：\\n  - 泛指复数或不可数名词时不加冠词：Plastic bottles are made of biodegradable materials. / Knowledge about the environment…\\n  - 特指（双方都知道是哪个）用 the：The plastic bottles that I threw out yesterday…\\n  - 第一次提到单数可数名词用 a/an：creates a problem\\n  - 固定用法：in the near future, in the wild, a high percentage of, the majority of"},{"id":"grammar-3","chapter":"grammar","title":"4. 比较句（Task 1 最常用，口语比较也用）","md":"- prefer doing A rather than doing B：I prefer spending time with my family on my birthday rather than spending time with them at New Year.\\n- not … as much as：Some people don't enjoy public holidays as much as other people I know.\\n- 比较时 compare 关注相同点，contrast 关注不同点\\n- more / fewer + 名词 + than：More females than males selected the bicycle.\\n- more / less + 形容词 + than；the most / least + 形容词\\n- 加强程度：much / far more powerful than\\n- as many as / not as many as\\n- **比较里加副词更准确**：\\n  - 差很多：significantly / considerably / substantially / far / much / many more：Significantly more people voted for the bicycle.\\n  - 差一点：slightly more women than men\\n  - 几乎一样：almost / nearly / practically as many … as：almost as many males as females\\n- **对比连接词**：whereas / while / but / although + 句子；in comparison with / compared with + 名词短语；However / By contrast 放句首\\n  - The arts and crafts society has the most 20–30 year-olds, but it is one of the least popular clubs with the older age group."},{"id":"grammar-4","chapter":"grammar","title":"5. 情态动词和建议（Task 2 写解决办法）","md":"- should 表示强烈建议，could 表示可能的办法\\n- One possibility is for the government to provide… / A further step is to…\\n- 加结果：By doing this, … / As a result, … / This would lead to… / This would enable them to…"},{"id":"grammar-5","chapter":"grammar","title":"6. 从句和复杂句","md":"- **定语从句**：Rosalind Franklin, **who** was so intelligent… / stepwells, **which** are found in…（who 指人，which 指物，逗号后不能用 that）\\n- **让步**：although / even though + 句子；despite + 名词或 -ing（despite being the most polluting）；whereas 表对比\\n- **if 条件句**：If nothing is done, CO2 emissions will increase.\\n- **which 从句补充信息**（Task 2 加细节的好工具）：\\n  - 补充说明，可以去掉，前后加逗号：News broadcasts about world disasters, **which** are now available 24 hours a day, can make people feel anxious.\\n  - which 指前面整句话，表示结果：People often allow the TV to do their thinking for them at home, **which** in turn has an impact on their mental performance at work.\\n  - 合并句子：Sometimes, computers make mistakes. This wastes valuable time. → Sometimes, computers make mistakes, **which** wastes valuable time.\\n- **让步句三种写法**：\\n  - Although + 句子，主句：Although people aged 41–50 were dominant on guided tours, they still accounted for one in ten backpackers.\\n  - Despite + 名词或 -ing：Despite being highly annoying, electronic gadgets are very useful.\\n  - 两句话：…. Nevertheless, … / …. However, …\\n  - 放在 although 后面的是你想弱化的一边，主句是你想强调的一边\\n- **假设句**：if, unless（除非，等于 if not）, provided / providing（只要）\\n  - If a nation nurtures the talents of its people, it will reap many benefits.\\n  - Unless there is an effort to keep traditional crafts alive, they will disappear.\\n  - 用 would / could / might 让观点不那么绝对：this might motivate some children to take up science.\\n- **with 连接句子**（with + 名词 + -ing）：There were several similarities, with the most and least important factors being the same. / Sales were upward, with the profit reaching a peak in December.\\n- **主谓一致**：主语中心词决定动词：The number of people who are suffering from stress **is** on the increase. / Predictions about … **are** often inaccurate. / The fact that people live longer **has** led to…\\n- **语序**：the period in question；From the graphs, it can be concluded that young people **are**…；among both men and women\\n- **with 独立结构**：nine storeys deep, **with** the last two **being** underwater"},{"id":"grammar-6","chapter":"grammar","title":"7. 常见搭配","md":"- 介词 of 后面用 -ing：the process of produc**ing** chocolate\\n- leave sb with sth：leaving fresh graduates with slim chances\\n- provide sb with sth：provide employees with their own computers\\n- spend time with sb / spend time doing sth\\n- 句子必须有谓语动词：…is that science **requires** a great deal of cognitive effort."},{"id":"grammar-7","chapter":"grammar","title":"8. 连接词","md":"- **按功能记连接词**（读文章时用来找路，Task 2 一定要用）：\\n  - 加内容 / 递进：and, also, in addition, moreover, furthermore, what's more, apart from this, not only… but also\\n  - 对比：but, however, whereas, by contrast, on the other hand\\n  - 让步：although, even though, despite, yet, even so\\n  - 原因：because, since, due to\\n  - 结果：so, therefore, and so, as a result, consequently, thus, hence, for this reason, which then led to, which leads to, which means that, as a consequence\\n  - 目的：in order to, so as to, so that, with the aim of, for the purpose of\\n  - 条件：if, unless, provided that\\n  - 举例：for example, for instance, such as\\n  - 结论：in conclusion, thus\\n  - 选择：or\\n  - Unless more funds are put into the health service soon, people will suffer.（条件）\\n  - The government opened three new hospitals so that they would be able to meet their targets.（目的）\\n- **结果和目的要分清**（两组词别混用）：\\n  - Some cities charge motorists to take their cars into the centre **in order to** reduce traffic. **As a result**, the air is cleaner.\\n- **顺序和时间词别混**：firstly / at first / initially 意思不同，at first 表示「起初（后来变了）」，不是列要点用的；recently / lately / not long ago 是最近，some time ago 是有一段时间以前；therefore 是结果，不是补充\\n- **流程和顺序**：First of all, After that, Following that, Subsequently, then, in turn, when, once, as soon as, before\\n  - 连两个被动句：After the parts of the car are assembled, the cars are exported. / Once the paper is collected, it is sent for recycling.\\n- **it / they / this / these 指代**（避免重复名词）：\\n  - it、this 指单数名词；they、these 指复数名词\\n  - this、these 常指上一句末尾的名词\\n  - this 还可以指整件事或一个过程：Studying history may trigger an interest in other subjects. **This**, in turn, may lead to other hobbies.\\n- **地点表达**（地图题）：north of the river / in the south-west of the town / beside the railway line / north-east of the lake\\n  - 介词：in the town of…；surrounded by trees；beside the railway line；in the north；ran from north to south；on the banks of the river；next to the sea；on the shores of the lake；just off the coastline\\n- **时间段替换**：Between 2000 and 2005 = Over the period = During the five-year period = From 2000 to 2005\\n- **反驳别人的观点**：Nevertheless, I feel… / However, I think… / Personally, I believe…\\n- **常见拼写错误**（写完要检查）：before, receive, studying, useful, personally, sufficient, definitely, different, choice, referred, gradually, which, occurred, peak, figures, approximately, fluctuated, exceeded, survey, average, improvement, motorcycle, occurring"},{"id":"grammar-8","chapter":"grammar","title":"9. 口语常用句型","md":"- **说喜欢和不喜欢，换着说**（不要老是 I like）：\\n  - 喜欢：I often enjoy… / I'm very keen on… / A lot of people like…\\n  - 不确定：I don't know if I like… / I'm not sure whether I like… / I don't know much about…\\n  - 不喜欢：I'm not a big fan of… / I'm not really interested in… / I hate… / I don't look forward to… / Not many people like…\\n- **用连接词把句子拉长**：and / but / so / because。I sometimes enjoy mountain climbing, but I prefer staying at home.\\n- **一次给三个理由**：I like going swimming. I like it because …, … and …\\n- **讲故事用的顺序词**：before, after, when, while, once, until, since, as, then, in order to。Once I had eaten, I took a tour bus to do a bit of shopping.\\n- **讲新闻用被动**：重点放在发生了什么，而不是谁做的。The earthquake destroyed a number of monuments. → A number of monuments **were destroyed** (by the earthquake).\\n- **would 问题用 would 回答**：Would you move house if you had the chance? → Yes, I'd love to move closer to the sea.\\n- **表达愿望和打算**：I'd like to… / I'd really love to… / I hope that one day I can… / I've always wanted to… / I wish that I could…\\n- **表达不想或不确定**：I'd probably hate… / I'm not convinced that I'd… / I'm not sure whether I'd… / There is no way I'd…\\n- **用从句把回答说长**（考官看语法多样性）：\\n  - which 补充评价：I once worked as a receptionist in a hotel, **which** was an interesting experience.\\n  - who 补充人：I've always been an admirer of Bill Gates, **who** is one of the world's most successful businesspeople.\\n  - when 补充时间：I remember how the economy used to be in the past, **when** people weren't as rich as they are now.\\n  - where 补充地点：I'd like to work in South Korea one day, **where** they are quick to adopt new technology.\\n- **口语里用缩写更自然**：I'd（I would）、wouldn't、don't、I'll（I will）、won't（will not）、should've（should have）、could've（could have）、That's（That is）\\n  - 虚拟过去：If I'd studied harder, I could've got the job.（如果当时……就能……）/ I should've taken a part-time job.（当时本该……）\\n- **过去和现在对比**：In the past, people **would / used to** get together with their families. Now, people like to…\\n- **让步（两边都说）**：Although / Even though / While + 一边，另一边：Although the festival gets very messy, it's such a colourful experience.\\n  - 也可以用：The problem is… / The trouble is… / The thing is… / The disadvantage of that is… / On the other hand, …\\n- **讲原因**：There are several reasons why… / The first reason is that… / Another point to consider is that… / The main reason is that… / Due to the fact that… / As…\\n- **提建议**：should（建议）、must（必须）、have to（不得不）：In order to improve our education system, the government should change the testing system.\\n- **讲差别**：The main difference between A and B is…\\n- **比较程度**：Celebrations were more / less important in the past than now because…\\n\\n---"},{"id":"speaking-0","chapter":"speaking","title":"口语考试流程（考官会做什么）","md":"- **开场（不到 1 分钟）**：考官说明自己的名字，问你的全名和怎么称呼，再核对证件（Can I see your identification, please?）\\n- **Part 1（4–5 分钟）**：考官问 2–3 个日常话题，每个话题 3–4 个问题（家乡、住处、学习或工作、爱好等）。考官照着题目念，不会和你聊天；你说得太长时考官会打断，这很正常\\n- **Part 2（3–4 分钟）**：考官给你一张题卡、一张纸和一支笔，说 You have one minute to prepare。1 分钟准备后，考官说 Please start speaking now，你说 1–2 分钟；到 2 分钟考官会叫停（Thank you）。之后可能问一两个简短问题\\n- **Part 3（4–5 分钟）**：考官围绕 Part 2 的话题问更深、更社会化的问题（为什么、怎么比较、将来会怎样）。考官会追问 Why? / Can you give an example?\\n- **结束**：考官说 That is the end of the speaking test，就可以离开了\\n- **注意**：\\n  - 听不清可以请考官重复一次（见下面的万能句型），不扣分\\n  - 考官不会告诉你答得好不好；面无表情是正常的\\n  - 回答要真实、自然；背的整段答案考官听得出来"},{"id":"speaking-1","chapter":"speaking","title":"各 Part 回答流程","md":"- **Part 1：回答 → 原因 → 例子或细节（2–3 句，约 15–20 秒）**\\n  - 每个回答先直接回答问题，再说一个原因，再加一个例子或细节\\n- **Part 2：用题卡上的提示点记笔记 → 按提示点顺序说 → 加过去的细节 → 说感受**\\n  1. 准备 1 分钟：每个提示点写 2–3 个关键词，再加一行\\"感受\\"（feelings）\\n  2. 开头一句点题：I'd like to talk about…\\n  3. 按提示点顺序说：who / what / when / where，每点说 2–3 句\\n  4. 讲经过时用过去时，加具体细节（时间、地点、天气、谁说了什么）\\n  5. 最后说感受和为什么重要：I felt… / It was special because…\\n  6. 还没到 2 分钟就继续补细节，用 What else? 问自己\\n  - 真实的 Part 2 长回答（官方评分 6.5 分，附考官评语）见本模块末尾「口语官方评分样本」\\n- **Part 3：观点 → 原因 → 例子 → 对比或另一面（4–6 句，约 40–60 秒）**\\n  - 真实的 Part 3 对话（官方评分 6 分和 7 分，附考官评语）见本模块末尾「口语官方评分样本」\\n  - 记住：Part 3 讲一般人和社会（people, society, the government），不只讲自己"},{"id":"speaking-2","chapter":"speaking","title":"答题公式","md":"- **Part 1 用 ARE**：Answer 直接回答，Reason 解释原因，Example 举个例子\\n- **Part 2 用 PREP**：Point 引出话题，Reason 原因，Example 具体细节和经过，Personal feelings 自己的感受；要说满 2 分钟\\n- **Part 3 用 PEEL**：Point 表明观点，Explanation 解释，Example 例子，Link 回扣问题\\n- 范文里的 Part 2「完美天气的一天」：按地点、天气、做了什么、为什么完美的顺序讲，多用温度、时间这些具体细节\\n- Part 1 好用开头：This is an interesting question for me. / To be honest, …\\n- Part 1 可以加过去和现在对比：A few years ago, I used to…, but these days…"},{"id":"speaking-3","chapter":"speaking","title":"Part 1 怎么答","md":"- Part 1 大多是 Wh- 问题（What、Who、When、Where、Why），Why 通常最后问，讲清楚就行，不用太细\\n- Yes / No 问题不能只答 Yes 或 No，至少再加两句解释（例：Yes, we live on the coast, and we can see the beach from our window – it's pretty nice.）\\n- 每个回答三句左右：回答、原因、例子\\n- 常见话题（家乡、住处、天气、购物、新闻、娱乐、运动）提前准备基本信息；可以自己围绕话题出问题来练\\n- 回答里用上连接词（and、but、so、because），长句子能让考官看到更复杂的语法\\n- **开场身份问答**（考官一定会问）：\\n  - Can you tell me your full name, please? 答：My name is…\\n  - And what can I call you? 答：Please call me…\\n  - Where do you come from? 答：I come from…\\n  - Can you show me your identification, please? 答：Of course. Here is my passport.\\n- **回答要加细节**：先回答，再加原因（because it is well connected to the city centre）或结果（so it is always noisy）\\n  - The neighbourhood where I live is very peaceful. The area is residential with tree-lined streets, no shops and not many cars.\\n- **说家乡和住处的好用句**：I used to live in… but now I… / I moved here… / It's a… place with… / What I like about it is… because… / The great thing about… is… / I suppose most people…\\n- 常考的熟悉话题：music, travel, transport, learning English, food, communication, sport, hobbies, TV, books；每个话题自己准备两个简单问题和答案\\n- **说喜好**：\\n  - 喜欢：I adore / I really enjoy / I'm fond of… / My favourite thing of all is… / Best of all, I like…\\n  - 更喜欢：I prefer A to B / I would rather live in town than in the countryside.\\n  - 不喜欢：I can't stand… / I dislike… / I hate… / … doesn't appeal to me.\\n  - 说原因：What appeals to me is that… / I find it relaxing. / The thing I like about… is that… / That's the great thing about…\\n- **被问到不会的东西也要回答**：别只说 No，说清楚为什么，再加过去或将来\\n  - Unfortunately not. I have very little practical ability. I tried when I was at school, but without success.\\n  - I wish I could. My parents made me take lessons when I was very young, but I just made a terrible noise.\\n  - That's not something I normally do. I probably used to when I was a lot younger, but my life's very busy now.\\n  - I'm afraid I have absolutely no skill in this area at all. But I might learn in the future.\\n- **Part 1 爱好题常见三连问**：Do you have any hobbies? → How and why did you first get involved in this activity? → How would you recommend it to another person?\\n- **运动题**：说喜欢或讨厌哪种运动时一定加原因\\n  - I prefer contact sports like football, not least because they're a good way to get rid of my aggression.\\n  - Swimming is the only individual sport I like, as I usually prefer being with other people.（团队运动以外的唯一例外）\\n  - I suppose I'm mostly interested in spectator sports, basically because I'm not a very energetic person."},{"id":"speaking-4","chapter":"speaking","title":"Part 2 的规则","md":"- 题目由考官给，不能自己选\\n- 有 1 分钟准备时间，笔记写在考官发的纸上\\n- 最多说 2 分钟，考官叫停之前要一直说\\n- 按题卡上的顺序讲，像讲故事：先交代背景，最后说自己的看法\\n- 可以给自己加问题（Where did I go? Who did I go with? Why do I remember it?），有更多话说\\n- 用顺序词把经过讲清楚，让考官听得懂从头到尾发生了什么\\n- 结束时总结一下前面说的\\n- 说完考官可能问一两个简短的追问（Would you…? Do you…? Is there…?），简单回答就好\\n- 讲新闻或事件时用被动语态，最后用上面的形容词说自己的感受"},{"id":"speaking-5","chapter":"speaking","title":"Part 2 怎么说满 2 分钟","md":"- 准备时间只有 1 分钟：笔记只写关键词，不写完整句子（比如 Victoria Falls / waterfall / 1,738 metres wide / rainbows / visit with family）\\n- 平时用手机计时练 1 分钟做笔记\\n- 先想清楚每个要点需要什么信息、举几个例子、用什么时态\\n- 说完提示问题后，用 What / Who / When / Where / How / Why 自己追问来扩展，多举例子、多做比较\\n- 卡住时用开头句接着说：I think I would be very interested in… / I've often thought about… / I wonder whether it would be fun to… / It would be fantastic if I could…\\n- **讲过去的事**：先用一个名词概括它（It was a rewarding experience. / It was an unforgettable moment.），再讲经过\\n- **1 分钟笔记最多写大约十个词**，用笔记开个头，然后围着笔记说\\n  - 例：题卡「描述一件你丢过的重要东西」，笔记可以写：→shop / →police / bag with shoulder strap / handbag / cards! / →newspaper\\n- **讲故事的顺序句**：Well, I should say first that… / To find it, I first… / After that, I… / Finally, I… / Looking back, I realize that… / In future I will (not)…\\n- **卡壳时的说法**：\\n  - 想词：Let me see, … / How shall I put it?\\n  - 回到正题：Now, where was I?\\n  - 强调：I should say…\\n- **说预防措施**：In future, I will put labels on my suitcases **in case** they get lost on the plane.\\n- 练习题卡：Describe a time when you were late for an event. / Describe an important thing that you lost and what happened when you lost it.\\n- **描述人（比如一位老师）的句子**：\\n  - 引出：The person I've chosen is… / I can remember… really well.\\n  - 外貌：Physically, he / she was… / He / She looked…\\n  - 性格：In terms of personality, … / Character-wise, he / she was…\\n  - 原因和影响：What… taught me was that… / I'll never forget him / her because…\\n- **两种做笔记的方法**：\\n  - 思维导图（中间写主题，往外分外貌、性格、习惯、特别之处、为什么是好老师）：写得快、词少、想法多，但会乱\\n  - 列清单：有条理、很整齐，但写得慢、词多\\n  - Part 2 只有 1 分钟，一般用思维导图更快\\n- 更多题卡：Describe a teacher you can remember from your schooldays. / Describe a person you know who has helped you in some way.\\n- **用 What 开头的句子强调重点**：\\n  - The open fields make the place so attractive. → What makes the place so attractive is the open fields.\\n  - The house is quiet because there are no neighbours. → What makes the house quiet is not having any neighbours.\\n  - 讲经历先用一句开头，再用 what 展开：The building that I like most is the old library. What I like most about it is the large windows.\\n  - 再用 because、as、since、with、which 补充原因和细节\\n- **描述地方时说出热情程度**：\\n  - 热情：caught my attention immediately / I have been fascinated by… / What makes the place so attractive is… / The reason why it appeals to me is…\\n  - 一般：is basically okay / is just about bearable\\n  - 加转折让答案更真实：…but it's in danger of being spoilt by tourists. / …but at times it can be lonely there. / …but sadly I haven't visited it for years.\\n- **描述动物**：说它是什么动物、性格（quite a character, very lively, friendly）、平时做什么（jump up, bark, curl up on my lap）、你和它一起做什么（take him for walks, feed her, groom her）\\n  - 引出回忆：The fondest memory I have is of… / What I remember most is… / The thing that sticks in my mind is…\\n  - 说不是你的宠物：Although it wasn't really my pet, … / To be honest, he wasn't my pet at all.\\n- **记笔记要实用**：按题卡顺序标 1、2、3、4，每点写几个关键词（mother, birthday / gold watch, waterproof / wore it all the time / expensive, quality），太短的缩写自己说的时候会想不起来\\n- 题卡：Describe an animal which belonged to you or someone you know. / Describe a present you received and that you liked very much.\\n- **描述地方和感受**：说它在哪里、你在那里做什么、给你什么感觉、对你有什么影响\\n  - 好的感受：It always relaxes me. / I always go whenever I feel down. / There's a freshness that feels good.\\n  - 不好的感受：There's something about the place that just feels oppressive. / I just want to get out as quick as I can.\\n  - 先想清楚生活里这几类地方：玩的、放松的、学习或工作的、吃饭的、一个人待的\\n- **Part 2 最后一点：总结你的看法**\\n  - 说为什么喜欢：I particularly liked / disliked this… because… / The main reason for my reaction was…\\n  - 说影响：Its main effect on me has been… / The influence this has had on me is…\\n  - 说学到什么：What I've learnt from this is… / This taught me an important lesson: …\\n  - 说为什么特别：I feel attached to this… because…\\n- 题卡：Describe a place which is important to you. / Describe a place where you spent a memorable holiday. / Describe an experience in which you tried something new. / Describe something special that you bought.\\n- **题卡：Describe a movie you enjoyed watching.**（What was the movie, and when did you watch it? / Who did you watch it with? / What was the movie about? / How did you feel while watching it?）\\n  - 开头：I would like to talk about a movie I enjoyed watching. It's called…, and I watched it… with…\\n  - 讲内容：The film portrays / depicts… / It's about… / There's a surprising plot twist near the end.\\n  - 讲感受：It was gripping from beginning to end. / It was an emotional roller coaster. / The main character was very relatable.\\n  - 收尾：Overall, it left a lasting impression on me because…\\n  - 用词别全用\\"高级词\\"，挑 3 到 4 个自己真会说的（gripping, plot twist, relatable, soundtrack）就够"},{"id":"speaking-6","chapter":"speaking","title":"Part 3 的五种问法","md":"- Part 3 问的是整个社会，不是你个人的经历\\n- **assess（评价）**：Have schools done enough to…?\\n- **compare（比较）**：Is there any difference between… now and in the past?\\n- **explain（解释原因）**：Why have businesses not done more to…?\\n- **predict（预测）**：What do you think will happen in the future?\\n- **suggest（建议）**：What can governments do to…?\\n- 回答时要给原因、因果和建议，并且两边都说（用让步句）\\n- 比较过去和现在的题：分四个角度想（过去重要的原因、现在重要的原因、过去不重要的原因、现在不重要的原因），多用不同时态\\n- **Part 3 题目的常见问法**（先学会认，自己也能出题练）：To what extent…? / In what ways…? / What are the main differences between…? / Which do you prefer…? / How…?\\n  - To what extent is shopping a form of relaxation?\\n  - In what ways have shopping habits been changed by globalization?\\n- **表达观点的句子**：In my view / opinion, … / Well, from my point of view, … / To my mind, … / It seems to me that… / Personally, I think… / My impression is that… / I suppose…\\n  - 读的时候重音放在 view、mind、seems、impression 这类词上\\n- **开放题和封闭题**：Yes/No 问题（Do you…? Are young people…?）多在 Part 1；What / How / Why 这种开放问题多在 Part 3\\n- **Part 3 好用开头**：\\n  - 问困难：There are many problems, but perhaps the greatest challenge is…\\n  - 问将来：The most likely development is that…\\n  - 问解决办法：By far the best way to tackle the situation is… because…\\n  - 问区别：The main difference is…\\n  - 展开时接：As a result, … / This is because… / Firstly, … / But perhaps the best solution is to… / Another point is… / This means that…\\n- **说好处和坏处**：\\n  - 好处：One definite plus is that… / The great advantage is… / On the one hand…\\n  - 坏处：One problem is that… / Another big disadvantage is… / A big minus is… / On the other (hand)…\\n  - 权衡总结：Weighing everything up, … / On balance, … / Taking everything into account, … / Overall, …\\n  - 例题：Is it better to go travelling on your own or with other people? / Which is more important in a job, money or job satisfaction?\\n- **比较题和评价题**：\\n  - 比较（Which is more important / Which provides the best…）：I think… is more important because… / This depends on whether you prefer…\\n  - 评价（To what extent / To what degree…）：To quite a large degree, because… / I think it's had a huge / minor influence. For example, … / I (don't) think it's a crucial factor because…\\n- **先说别人的看法，再说自己的**：\\n  - 引出别人：Some people say that… / It is often argued that… / Many people believe that…\\n  - 反驳：But I don't think that… / However, I'm not convinced… / I'd disagree with that because…\\n  - 例题：Should governments subsidize scientific research? / To what extent would it be better to lead a simpler life, without advanced technology?\\n- **认出意思相同的问题**：考官换个问法，答案内容可以一样\\n  - In what ways are sport and health linked? = Are sport and health connected? If so, how?\\n  - What are the main causes of ill-health in the modern world? = Which factors are contributing to low levels of health today?\\n  - How is the modern diet different from the diet of the past? = How is the food we eat different from the food eaten by previous generations?\\n- **强调主要观点**：It's mostly because of… / The main cause seems to be… / I'd say… is the key thing. / I think the most effective way is… / I suppose the best way is… / It's obvious that…\\n- **想不出答案时争取时间**：可以承认问题难，然后尽量答，别要求换题\\n  - That's a difficult question. Let me think… / I've never really thought about that before, but… / That's an interesting question. I suppose…\\n- **原因要放在一般层面**：Part 3 不说\\"我\\"，说一般人：Doing sport makes people more mentally alert. / Sport is a good way to meet new people.\\n- 例题：How is good health related to education and wealth? / What dangers are associated with exercise and sport? / How can individuals best contribute to society?"},{"id":"speaking-7","chapter":"speaking","title":"发音","md":"- **单词重音**：记词时顺便记重音在哪个音节\\n  - plea·sant（重音在前）、dy·NA·mic、pea·ceful、ba·ngalow、de·TACHED、o·ver·PRICED\\n  - a**PART**ment、ac**com**mo**DA**tion、**AR**chitecture、con**STRUC**tion、**ES**calators、in**HA**bitants、**MON**ument、mu**SE**um、resi**DEN**tial、**STA**dium、**COUN**tryside、en**VI**ronment、ge**OG**raphy、re**LI**gion、**TEM**peratures、**SCE**nery\\n- **词性变了重音会变**：IMagine → imagiNAtion，MOtivate → motiVAtion，OPtimist → optiMIStic，ARtist → arTIStic，PESsimist → pessiMIStic\\n- **复合形容词的重音**：放在名词前时重音在后面（a well-PAID accountant），单独用或放在 be 后面时两个部分都重读（Most accountants are WELL-PAID）；同类的还有 well-dressed, well-qualified, easy-going, fair-minded\\n- **can 和 can't**：can 在句子里通常读得又轻又短（/kən/），can't 读得重而且长（/kɑːnt/），听力里靠这个区分\\n- **like 和 'd like**：I like listening to rock music.（平时就喜欢）/ I'd like to try a new hobby.（现在想做），'d 很轻，要仔细听\\n- **弱读**：the 在辅音前读 /ðə/，在元音前读 /ði/（the arts）；that、there、some 不重要时读得很轻，强调时才读重\\n- **缩写读法**：would 和 will 常缩成 I'd、I'll，听起来更自然\\n- **句子重音**：实词（名词、动词、形容词）读重，虚词（the、of、a）读轻：I think that **rowing** is a **great sport** if you want to stay **fit** and **healthy**.\\n- **语调表达感情**：平平地读听起来很无聊；说开心的事语调要有起伏：My **favourite** sport is **hockey**. It's **amazing**!\\n- **不发音的字母**：scenic 的 c、business 的 i、foreigner 的 g、should 的 l、guest 的 u、autumn 的 n、honest 的 h、light 的 gh、doubt 的 b、castle 的 t、yoghurt 的 h\\n- **对比重音**：比较两样东西时，把要对比的关键词读重，让考官听出对比；纠正或强调信息时，重读要纠正的那个词\\n  - 比较：This holiday is much more **exciting** than **that** holiday.\\n  - Thirty minutes daily is good. → THIRTY（不是 sixty）/ DAILY（不是 weekly）\\n  - Fresh fruit is good for EVERYONE.（不只是孩子）/ FRESH fruit…（不是冷冻或罐头的）\\n  - 纠正别人：Men spend thirty minutes a DAY on sport, not a week.\\n  - 练法：用自己的例子写 3 个比较句，大声读，重读对比的词\\n- **过去式 -ed 的三种读法**：\\n  - /t/：在 p、k、s、sh、ch、f 这类清音后面：jumped, liked, watched, camped, picnicked, panicked\\n  - /d/：在元音和浊音后面：tried, climbed, arrived, enjoyed\\n  - /ɪd/：在 t 和 d 后面多一个音节：started, landed, collected\\n  - 例句：We started our walk at 2 p.m. We climbed the cliffs and watched the sun set."},{"id":"speaking-8","chapter":"speaking","title":"好用表达","md":"| 表达 | 意思 |\\n|---|---|\\n| a bit far-fetched | 有点不太可信 |\\n| slip one's mind | 一下子忘了 |\\n| foster deep reflection | 引发深刻思考 |\\n| brush aside nonsense | 把胡说八道放一边 |\\n| When it comes to this topic, the first thing that pops into my mind is… | 说到这个话题，我第一个想到的是…… |\\n| find oneself in a repetitive situation | 发现自己陷入重复单调的处境 |\\n| outgoing, open-minded, sense of humor, good fun to be around | 外向，思想开放，幽默感，相处起来很有趣（描述人） |\\n| I'd like to talk about… / I've known him for about 10 years | Part 2 开头 |"},{"id":"speaking-9","chapter":"speaking","title":"表达观点和同意不同意","md":"- 很确定：certainly, clearly, definitely, indeed, no doubt, of course, surely, will\\n- 不太确定：likely, almost, maybe, might, seemingly, perhaps, occasionally, unlikely\\n- 同意：That's right. / That's also how I feel about it. / I have to side with you on that one. / Me neither.（同意否定句）\\n- 不同意：That's incorrect. / I beg to differ. / I'm afraid I don't share that point of view.\\n- 半同意：You might have a point there. / I'm not sure about that.\\n- 加强语气：I **just** don't share that point of view. / That's **totally** incorrect. / I **definitely** have to side with you on that one. / That's **100%** true.\\n- 很确定和不太确定的对比：If things do not improve quickly, there is **no doubt** that the environment **will** suffer.（确定）/ it is **possible** that the environment **might** suffer.（谨慎）"},{"id":"speaking-10","chapter":"speaking","title":"Part 2 题卡汇总","md":"- **人物**：Describe a teacher you can remember from your schooldays. / Describe a person you know who has helped you in some way. / Describe a successful businessperson you would like to meet.\\n- **物品**：Describe an important thing that you lost and what happened when you lost it. / Describe a present you received and that you liked very much. / Describe something special that you bought. / Describe an animal which belonged to you or someone you know.\\n- **地方**：Describe a place which is important to you. / Describe a place where you spent a memorable holiday. / Describe a place famous for its natural beauty. / Describe a place of natural beauty you have visited.\\n- **事件和经历**：Describe a time when you were late for an event. / Describe an experience in which you tried something new. / Describe a memorable celebration. / Describe a public holiday in your country. / Describe a sports event you watched or attended. / Describe an exciting journey you once took. / Describe a day with perfect weather.（范文思路见「答题公式」）\\n- **媒体和娱乐**：Describe a movie you enjoyed watching. / Describe a news story you read or saw. / Describe a hobby you enjoy.\\n- **工作和社会**：Describe a job you would like to do for a day. / Describe a successful business in your country. / Describe an environmental issue facing your country. / Describe a problem with the education system in your country."},{"id":"speaking-11","chapter":"speaking","title":"按提问类型的句型","md":"- **喜好和偏好**（Do you like…? / Which do you prefer…?）\\n  - I'm really into… / I'm quite keen on… / I'd rather… than… / I prefer… to… because…\\n  - 例：I prefer tea to coffee because coffee keeps me awake at night.\\n- **频率和习惯**（How often do you…? / What do you usually do…?）\\n  - I usually… / I tend to… / Once or twice a week, I… / Hardly ever. / Every now and then, I…\\n  - 例：I tend to go swimming once or twice a week, usually on weekend mornings.\\n- **过去的经历**（Have you ever…? / When did you last…?）\\n  - Yes, I have. I remember when I… / The last time I… was… / When I was a child, I used to…\\n  - 例：The last time I went to the cinema was about a month ago, with my best friend.\\n- **将来和计划**（What do you plan to…? / Would you like to…?）\\n  - I'm planning to… / I'm hoping to… / I'd love to… one day. / If I have the chance, I will…\\n  - 例：I'm hoping to travel to Japan next year to see the cherry blossoms.\\n- **过去和现在比较**（Is it different now from the past?）\\n  - In the past, people used to…, but nowadays… / Compared with… years ago, … / … has changed a lot.\\n  - 例：In the past, people used to write letters, but nowadays most people send messages on their phones.\\n- **描述人**：The person I'd like to describe is… / He's the kind of person who… / What I admire most about her is…\\n  - 例：My aunt is the kind of person who always helps others without being asked.\\n- **描述地方**：It's located in… / It's famous for… / What I like most about it is… / It's the perfect place to…\\n  - 例：It's located near the sea and it's famous for its fresh seafood.\\n- **描述物品**：It's made of… / It's about the size of… / I use it to… / It means a lot to me because…\\n  - 例：It's a small wooden box, about the size of my hand, and I use it to keep old photos.\\n- **描述事件**：It happened when… / At first… then… / In the end… / I'll never forget it because…\\n  - 例：It happened when I was fifteen. At first I was nervous, but in the end I won the race.\\n- **观点和同意不同意**（Do you think…? / Do you agree…?）\\n  - Personally, I believe… / I totally agree, because… / I see what you mean, but… / I'm not sure I agree, because…\\n  - 例：I see what you mean, but I think exams are still the fairest way to test students.\\n- **优点和缺点**（What are the advantages of…?）\\n  - The biggest advantage is that… / Another benefit is… / The downside is that… / On the other hand…\\n  - 例：The biggest advantage of living alone is freedom. The downside is that it can be lonely.\\n- **原因和解决办法**（Why…? / What can be done…?）\\n  - I think the main reason is… / This is mainly because… / One way to solve this is to… / The government could…\\n  - 例：One way to solve this is to build more cycle lanes, so that people can ride safely.\\n- **预测将来**（What will… be like in the future?）\\n  - I expect that… / It's likely that… / In the next ten years, … will probably… / I doubt that…\\n  - 例：It's likely that more people will work from home in the next ten years.\\n- **假设问题**（What would you do if…? / If you could…?）\\n  - If I had the chance, I would… / I'd probably… / If that happened, I think I'd…\\n  - 例：If I could live anywhere, I'd probably choose a small town by the sea."},{"id":"speaking-12","chapter":"speaking","title":"口语万能句型（争取时间、澄清、自我纠正、举例、收尾）","md":"- **争取思考时间**：Well, let me think… / That's an interesting question. / I've never really thought about that, but… / It's hard to say, but I suppose…\\n- **请考官重复或澄清**：Sorry, could you repeat the question, please? / Sorry, could you say that again? / Do you mean…?\\n  - 注意：Part 1 考官一般只会重复问题，不解释词的意思，所以听不懂也要先猜着答；Part 3 可以请考官换个说法（Could you put that another way?）\\n- **自我纠正**：Sorry, I mean… / Or rather… / What I'm trying to say is…\\n  - 例：I went there in 2019 – sorry, I mean 2018.\\n- **想不起一个词时换个说法**：It's a kind of… / It's something you use to… / I'm not sure what it's called, but it's…\\n  - 例：I'm not sure what it's called, but it's a tool you use to open bottles.\\n- **举例子**：For example, … / For instance, … / Take… for example. / A good example is…\\n  - 例：Take my cousin for example. She learned to cook by watching videos online.\\n- **补充更多内容**：On top of that, … / What's more, … / Another thing is that…\\n- **收尾**：So, that's why I… / Overall, I'd say… / So, all in all, …\\n  - 例：So, all in all, I'd say it was one of the best days of my life."},{"id":"reading-0","chapter":"reading","title":"阅读总体策略（60 分钟三篇文章）","md":"- **时间**：每篇约 20 分钟，第一篇最简单、第三篇最难；第一篇尽量 17–18 分钟做完，给第三篇多留时间。阅读没有额外誊写时间，要边做边把答案写到答题卡上\\n- **每篇的做题顺序**：\\n  1. 花 1–2 分钟略读：看标题、副标题、每段第一句，知道文章大意和每段在讲什么\\n  2. 先看题目要求：是哪几种题型、字数限制是多少\\n  3. 先做\\"按顺序出题\\"的题（填空、判断、选择、简答），再做\\"不按顺序\\"的题（段落信息匹配、段落标题、人名匹配）\\n  4. 一道题找了 1–2 分钟还找不到，就先猜一个答案、做个记号，往下做\\n- **定位方法**：在题目里划关键词，优先用不会被改写的词（人名、地名、数字、年份、专有名词）去扫读；其他词要想同义说法（children → young people，increase → rise）\\n- **答案顺序速查**：\\n  - 一般按原文顺序：句子填空、摘要填空（无词表）、表格和流程图填空、判断题、选择题、简答题、图表标注\\n  - 不按原文顺序：段落信息匹配、段落标题、人名观点匹配、分类题、句子结尾匹配（结尾选项不按顺序，但题目开头一般按顺序）\\n  - 利用顺序：第 1 题和第 3 题的位置找到了，第 2 题就在它们之间\\n- **字数限制**：看清 ONE WORD ONLY / NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS / ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER；超字数直接算错（详细规则见「十、考试规则」）\\n- **不留空**：答错不扣分，最后 1 分钟把所有空着的题都猜一个"},{"id":"reading-1","chapter":"reading","title":"通用做法（扫读、略读、预测、定位）","md":"- **扫读（scanning）**：只找一个词或短语，不是读懂全文\\n  - 只找具体的词，一次找一个；找的时候不去想意思，用笔带着眼睛走，找到就划线\\n  - 先找最好认的：大写字母（人名、地名，如 Mali、Botswana）和数字最容易一眼找到\\n  - 几种扫法：从右下往左上斜着扫、从下往上竖着扫、之字形扫、一行从右到左一行从左到右；挑一种别逐词读\\n  - 用「段落 + 首字母 + 意思」找同义词：比如 B 段里 t 开头、意思是 happening 的词就是 taking place\\n  - **按意思扫读（scanning for meaning）**：要找的词原文里不一定有，先自己想几个同义说法再扫（negative consequence = unfortunate outcome，indispensable part = vital role，alternative therapy = non-conventional medicine，psychological well-being = good mental health，congenial surroundings = pleasant environment，enormous progress = considerable improvement）\\n  - **找句子的功能**：题目说 suggestion、condition 这种词原文不会直接出现，要扫能表示它的词：建议看 should, would be a good start, need to；条件看 if, provided (that), unless；结论看 thus, so, after all；例子看 for example, such as；问题看 anxiety, problem, drain\\n- **略读（skimming）**：快速抓大意，不看每个词。只看名词和动词这种实词，跳过 a, the, in, of；不要读太细\\n  - 先读标题，猜文章里会出现哪些词（比如标题有 engineers，就会出现 construction, bridges, railway, projects）\\n  - 用来做段落标题匹配：每段只扫关键词，判断这段在讲什么\\n  - 判断一段是「问题和解决」还是「原因和结果」：看 the causes of, have led to, as a result 这类词\\n- **预测（predicting）**：先读标题和题目，用题目信息预测文章内容；英语文章有固定顺序，常常是先讲问题、再讲在哪里出现、再讲原因、最后讲将来\\n- **定位顺序**：先看标题，再看题目，然后回原文定位（可以在题目旁标上 P1 L1 这样的段落和行号）\\n- **同义改写**：选项和题目常常是原文的同义改写，不是原词照搬，所以找的是意思，不是一模一样的词（remove water = pumped water out of；colliding = collisions；dirty, crowded = pollution, overcrowded）\\n- **数字题要特别小心**：原文同一处常出现两个年份或数字，要看清数字属于哪一年\\n- **时间不够时**：先做填空和判断，再做匹配题（时间分配见「十、考试规则」）"},{"id":"reading-2","chapter":"reading","title":"判断题（TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN 和 YES / NO / NOT GIVEN）","md":"- **两种题的区别**：TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN 问文中信息，YES / NO / NOT GIVEN 问作者观点（文章是作者在表达看法时用这种题），判断方法一样\\n- **基本规则**：原文意思相反选 FALSE / NO；原文根本没说选 NOT GIVEN（比如题目说 more people than predicted，原文没提预测，就是 NOT GIVEN）\\n- **做题步骤**：\\n  1. 先读标题，扫一遍题目，用它们预测文章讲什么\\n  2. 在题目里划出认识、能用来扫读的词（最好是大写、数字这种不会被改写的词）\\n  3. 找出比较和限定词，尤其是副词和形容词（better, only, more, slowly, faster, minor, more effective），它们最常决定 FALSE 还是 NOT GIVEN\\n  4. 找出因果说法（is linked to, has resulted in, makes it unnecessary, due to, put … down to 归因于），检查原文是不是真的给了这个原因\\n  5. 先预测答案\\n  6. 在原文找到扫读词，再读它前后的句子定答案\\n- **其他技巧**：题目顺序和原文顺序一样；找 must、should、could，再在原文找类似的说法；划出带负面意思的词（boring, reluctance, lack of）\\n- **比较句判断流程**：\\n  - 题目和原文都提到两样东西，但原文没有比较，选 NOT GIVEN（covers more of Mali than Chad）\\n  - 题目提到两样东西，原文只提到一样，选 NOT GIVEN\\n  - 原文也比较了，但方向反了（题目说 A 比 B 大，原文说 B 比 A 大），选 FALSE\\n  - 原文比较的方向一样，选 TRUE\\n- **常见 NOT GIVEN**：题目做了比较，原文没比较；题目说将来会怎样或另有计划，原文没提\\n- **判断为什么是 NOT GIVEN 时，问自己**：作者有没有给出这个原因？有没有说这个结果？有没有做这个比较？比如原文只说「很多买的电器用不着」，题目说「英国比欧洲其他国家买得多」，原文没比较，就是 NOT GIVEN\\n- **作者观点题（YES / NO）的陷阱**：\\n  - 题目说 only（只有）而原文说 generally（普遍），要小心，常常是 NO\\n  - 作者举出别人的看法（some journalists take the view that…）不等于作者自己同意，要看作者后面怎么评价\\n  - 题目说「只能带来一点点提高」（can only lead to a slight improvement），原文说 radically improved，就是 NO\\n- **先分清事实和观点**：\\n  - 事实：Governments help vulnerable people in society. / The survey revealed that…\\n  - 观点：Governments **should** do more… / **Foolishly**, some employees… / It would, **I feel**, be a good idea…\\n  - 观点的四种标志：限定副词（unfortunately, foolishly, clearly）、限定形容词（better, inevitable）、因果（because, if… would）、情态动词（should, must, could）"},{"id":"reading-3","chapter":"reading","title":"句子填空和 ONE WORD ONLY 填空","md":"- **三步**：先看要填什么词性，再看字数限制，再找空前后的关键词\\n- **字数限制**：ONE WORD ONLY、ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER、NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS，多写一个词就错（书写规则见「十、考试规则」）\\n- **判断词性**：先判断空格要形容词还是名词（described as ___ 多半是形容词，the death of the surrounding ___ 是名词）；先问自己\\"这个空要填一样什么东西\\"（名词）还是\\"什么样\\"（形容词）\\n- **回原文**：用题目里的词回原文扫读，答案照抄原文的词；答案一般按原文顺序出现\\n- **ONE WORD ONLY**：只能填一个词，而且是原文里的原词；别直接抄题目附近已经出现过的词\\n- **做题步骤**：\\n  1. 读题目要求，圈出字数限制\\n  2. 读句子，判断空格要填的词性和意思类型（人、地点、数字、东西、形容词）\\n  3. 划出句子里的关键词，想 1–2 个同义说法\\n  4. 回原文找到对应的句子，把原文的词填进去\\n  5. 把填好的句子读一遍，检查语法和单复数（a ___ 后面是单数，many ___ 后面是复数）\\n- **陷阱**：原文附近有两个都\\"像答案\\"的词时，看哪个能和空格前后的词搭配；原文是复数（books），答案写单数就错；把原文的词改了词形也会错"},{"id":"reading-4","chapter":"reading","title":"摘要填空（有词表、无词表、A–K 字母选项）","md":"- **先找对应段落**：用摘要开头和结尾的词找出摘要对应原文哪一段，只在那一段里找答案，不要读全文\\n- **先猜再找**：先不看原文，略读摘要，自己猜每个空的意思和词性（数量、顺序、电子东西、结果……；形容词、名词、动词），可以在空处默念 blank；用上下文和常识帮忙（I think it's a noun / a verb here）\\n- **带词表（A–J / A–K 选字母）**：\\n  - 选项是原文意思的概括，常常是同义改写（did a deal with = strategic alliance；fritter away as much as half of their time = wasting significant amounts of time）\\n  - 先判断每个空的词性（as 后面、the greatest 后面要名词，be 后面常是形容词；或者要名词还是形容词加名词），把选项按词性分组，能排除一半，再用意思排除\\n  - 从词表里找跟空格前后能搭配的词；词表里意思相反的一对（beneficial effect / negative impact，greater role / lesser role）通常只有一个对，可以先排除一个\\n  - 最后读原文那一段确认\\n- **没有词表**：猜完再回原文找原词，一定要回原文检查；字数限制 ONE word only 时只能填一个原文的词"},{"id":"reading-5","chapter":"reading","title":"表格填空和流程图填空","md":"- **表格填空**：先看表头（横的和竖的）弄清表格在比较什么，表头往往就是文章的结构；注意字数限制\\n- **流程图填空**：流程图讲步骤和顺序，常用 firstly, at first, after that, subsequently, following that, in the next phase, finally 这类词定位；流程图里常用笔记式写法，省掉 is / are 和冠词（Ethanol produced once filtering completed.）"},{"id":"reading-6","chapter":"reading","title":"图表标注和地图标注","md":"- **图表标注（labelling a diagram）**：\\n  - 先看图，判断每个空要什么词（名词多）；用图和常识先猜空里大概是什么（温度、物质、动作）\\n  - 在原文找描述这个图的那一段，再扫读确认；答案一般按图上的编号顺序出现\\n  - 注意 TWO WORDS or a number 这种字数限制\\n- **地图标注（labelling a map）**：\\n  - 先找地图上的参照点（You are here、Main 这类），看清指北方向\\n  - 在原文给地名画框，划出方位词：north of, south-east corner, just east of, opposite, behind, beyond, on the same level as, directly behind\\n  - 按原文顺序一个一个对到地图上，每次只做一个，别同时做好几个"},{"id":"reading-7","chapter":"reading","title":"简答题（Short Answer Questions）","md":"- 先划出题目里的疑问词（What kind / Which area / What shape / How many / What lies behind），它告诉你答案是什么类型\\n- 用题目里的地名、人名去扫读，答案一般按原文顺序出现，直接抄原文的词，不超过字数限制\\n- **做题步骤**：1. 圈出疑问词和字数限制；2. 预测答案类型（When → 时间，How many → 数字，Who → 人）；3. 用关键词定位；4. 找到后只抄回答问题必需的那几个词\\n- **陷阱**：答案要回答问题本身，不要多抄句子里的修饰词（问 What material，答 wood，不写 a kind of light wood）；同一句里可能有两个数字，要看哪个对应题目"},{"id":"reading-8","chapter":"reading","title":"段落标题题（List of Headings）","md":"- **做题五步**：\\n  1. 先略读所有标题，大概知道文章讲什么，留意重复出现的词\\n  2. 划出标题里的组织词，看它们之间的联系和逻辑顺序\\n  3. 预测每个标题大概对应哪一段\\n  4. 略读段落（先读每段第一二句和末句），核对预测，完成匹配\\n  5. 最后按段落顺序把选的标题连起来读一遍，看顺不顺\\n- **标题里的组织词（organizing words）告诉你这段是哪种内容**：effect / consequence / impact（结果）、causes / reasons / factors（原因）、problem（问题）、types（种类）、belief（看法）、criticism（批评）、prediction / future（将来）\\n- **用标题猜整篇文章的结构**：比如先讲问题，再讲造成问题的原因，最后讲后果；可以先按文章常见顺序猜标题顺序\\n- **组织词常常成对出现，意思相近**：advantage = benefit，aim = purpose = goal = objective，consequence = outcome = effect，difference = discrepancy，difficulty = problem = obstacle，factor = influence，hazard = risk，characteristic = feature，analysis = explanation = interpretation，connection = link = bond = relationship = correlation = relation = association（动词 connected = linked = related = associated）；其他常见的还有 role, strategies, action, reservations（保留意见）, outline（概述）\\n- **细小区别**：solely / alone（只靠一种）和 accompanied by（再加别的）\\n- **标题里的复数很重要**：interpretations、ways of defining 说明这段会讲好几种说法或好几个例子\\n- **一段的结构可以画成图**：比如「各种定义方法」下面跟三个例子，那这段的标题就是概括这三个例子的那个\\n- **略读一段时只看表达意思的词**，然后在两个标题里选：比如一段讲正规教育、校外教育、自学成才的人，标题选 The impact of education outside formal settings，而不是 The importance of academic education\\n- **排除**：例子里已经用掉的标题不能再选；有些标题是干扰项，用不上；做完后看剩下没用的标题，想想为什么不合适，能帮你检查答案\\n- **自己概括标题要尽量短**：The paragraph describes the outcome of the research on stem cells → The outcome of stem cell research；The section explains how culture and wealth are linked → The link between culture and wealth"},{"id":"reading-9","chapter":"reading","title":"段落信息匹配和短语匹配（Which paragraph contains…）","md":"- **题目是概括性的说法**（reference to…, examples of…, mention of…, how someone accounted for…），原文是具体内容；先想清楚题目要找\\"例子\\"\\"研究结果\\"\\"某人的解释\\"还是\\"提到某类人\\"\\n- **同一个字母可以用好几次**（NB You may use any letter / paragraph more than once），有的段落一次都不用\\n- **先读题目抓关键词再扫段落**；这种题顺序打乱，建议放在同一篇的其他题后面做，那时已经熟悉文章了\\n- **短语匹配（matching phrases）四步**：\\n  1. 先划出短语里的组织词（the idea that, the fact that, ways of），判断短语对应整段还是段里的一部分：various strategies（各种方法）这种复数概括词一般对应整段；a comparison、a cause of 这种只对应段里的一两句话\\n  2. 判断信息大概在段落开头、中间还是结尾\\n  3. 扫读短语里的词或它们的同义词\\n  4. 不相关的信息直接跳过"},{"id":"reading-10","chapter":"reading","title":"句子结尾匹配（Matching Sentence Endings）","md":"- 先把开头里的扫读词圈出来（人名、地名、年份）\\n- 看结尾之间的关系：哪些是原因、哪些是结果、哪些是例子（led to, meant, was a response to 表示结果或因果）\\n- 先预测哪个开头配哪个结尾，再把语法、搭配、意思接不上的结尾排除；先看语法能不能接上，再找同义替换\\n- 最后回原文核对；有的结尾是干扰项，用不上\\n- **陷阱**：有的结尾语法上能接上、意思也对，但原文没这么说，这种也不能选；题目的开头一般按原文顺序出现，可以用这一点缩小查找范围"},{"id":"reading-11","chapter":"reading","title":"人名（观点）匹配题","md":"- 一个字母可以用多次\\n- **四步**：1. 在原文扫出每个名字，画个框；2. 框住的范围就是要找他观点、发现的地方；3. 看他的观点写在名字前面还是后面；4. 再读选项找对应的那一个\\n- 选项是原文的同义改写，常常把意思反过来设陷阱（比如原文是 practical 好、academic 差，选项故意写成 academic 好、practical 差）\\n- **陷阱**：\\n  - 同一个人在文章里可能出现好几次，观点分散在不同段落，要把他每次出现的地方都看一遍\\n  - 原文用 he / she / the researcher 指代这个人，别只找名字\\n  - 选项可能是别人的观点，只是放在这个人名附近"},{"id":"reading-12","chapter":"reading","title":"分类题（Classifying Information）","md":"- 比如把特点分到 A 干蒸汽、B 闪蒸、C 双循环、D 全部\\n- 先在原文给每一类画框标上 A、B、C，再一题一题对，不要同时做\\n- 一个特点几类都有，就选 all of them\\n- 按年代分类（between 1950 and 1990 / after 2005）时，先把原文的年份全圈出来"},{"id":"reading-13","chapter":"reading","title":"选择题（单选、选两个、选三个观点、全文标题）","md":"- **做题五步**：\\n  1. 做题前先读标题和题目，预测答案大概在文章哪里\\n  2. 用前面题目学到的信息先猜答案\\n  3. 看题干和选项是什么关系（比如原因和结果）\\n  4. 用题干里的扫读词找到对应段落；题目里点名某个人（如 Eyre、Ericsson），先在原文找到这个人名，再读他前后的几句话\\n  5. 读那一段，把原文意思和选项里的同义改写对上\\n- **题干的固定说法**，看到就知道考什么：\\n  - mainly, usually, the majority, the most：考限定词，选「主要」的那个，不选只是提到的\\n  - leads to, ensures that, means that, causes：考结果\\n  - because, as a result of, is caused by：考原因\\n  - is used for, the main purpose of … is to：考用途或目的\\n  - The writer refers to … to show / illustrate, … is an example of：考例子说明了什么观点；看例子前后作者的评价句\\n  - In order to achieve…：考为了达到目的用什么办法\\n  - The writer concludes / believes that, the writer's main point is：考全文观点，答案一般在最后一段；先看标题猜作者态度\\n  - main purpose（作者写这段的主要目的）：看整段在干什么，不是某一句话的细节\\n  - the penultimate paragraph = 倒数第二段\\n- **排除选项**：一个跟作者意思相反，另外两个原文没提，剩下的才是同义改写原文的那个；排除说得太绝对的选项（should be totally banned）\\n- **作者态度**：原文的评价词（delicious details, doesn't quite hit the mark, do justice to）是判断作者态度的关键\\n- **选 TWO（Choose TWO letters）**：五个选项里只有两个在原文有依据；先在原文找到相关段落，每个选项逐个核对，把原文没提的和意思相反的排除；选项里常有\\"文中提到了一部分但不是题目问的\\"干扰项\\n- **选三个观点（selecting statements）**：先略读所有选项，判断答案大概在文章哪一部分；用人名、群体词（students, academics, employers）扫读，不要用全文到处都有的词（比如 electronic gadgets）去扫；小心 definitely、totally、fails to 这种说得太绝对的选项，原文常常没说这么满\\n- **选全文标题（global multiple choice）**：选能概括全文的，不选只讲某一段的（比如只讲历史或只讲一个例子的选项）"},{"id":"reading-14","chapter":"reading","title":"阅读文章类型","md":"- **历史发展类**（如伦敦地铁的历史）：按时间顺序，题目也大致按顺序出\\n- **说明类**（如体育场的过去、现在和未来）：每段一个功能，适合段落信息匹配\\n- **书评类**（如一本讲追捕查理二世的历史书）：作者观点多，常考 YES / NO / NOT GIVEN 和作者态度\\n\\n---"},{"id":"rules-0","chapter":"rules","title":"考试时间和顺序","md":"- **听力**：约 30 分钟，4 个部分，40 题，录音只放一遍。纸笔考最后有 10 分钟把答案誊到答题卡；机考没有誊写时间，只有约 2 分钟检查\\n- **阅读**：60 分钟，3 篇文章，40 题，**没有额外誊写时间**。每篇大约 20 分钟，第三篇最难，别在前面的一道题上卡太久，不会的先猜一个\\n- **写作**：总共 60 分钟，两篇连着写，没人提醒换题。建议 Task 1 用 20 分钟，Task 2 用 40 分钟；Task 2 的分数占比是 Task 1 的两倍，所以很多人先写 Task 2\\n- **口语**：11 到 14 分钟。Part 1 约 4–5 分钟；Part 2 准备 1 分钟、说 1–2 分钟；Part 3 约 4–5 分钟\\n- 听力、阅读、写作同一天考，口语可能在同一天或前后几天"},{"id":"rules-1","chapter":"rules","title":"答案书写规则（听力和阅读）","md":"- **字数限制最重要**：NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER = 最多两个词加一个数字；超了直接算错\\n  - 带连字符的词算一个词（well-known）；数字可以写阿拉伯数字（15 不用写 fifteen）\\n- **拼写错了不给分**：英式、美式拼写都可以（colour / color）\\n- **单复数要对**：原文是 books，写 book 就错\\n- **只写原文里的词**：填空题的答案一般是原文或录音里的原词，不用自己改词形\\n- **大小写**：全部大写或全部小写都可以，纸笔考写全大写最清楚\\n- **不要空着**：答错不扣分，不会的一定要猜一个\\n- 日期可以写 15 March、March 15 或 15/3；时间写 9:30 或 9.30 都行"},{"id":"rules-2","chapter":"rules","title":"评分标准（四项各占 25%，6 分要做到什么）","md":"- **写作四项**：\\n  - 完成任务（Task Achievement / Task Response）：Task 1 有概括段、挑出主要特点；Task 2 回应题目的每一部分，立场清楚，观点有展开（有些可以展开得不够充分）\\n  - 连贯和衔接（Coherence and Cohesion）：分段清楚、有整体顺序；会用连接词，但用得有点机械或偶尔用错也还能拿 6\\n  - 词汇（Lexical Resource）：词汇量够完成题目；会试着用一些不常见的词，有些拼写或搭配错误但不影响理解\\n  - 语法（Grammatical Range and Accuracy）：简单句和复杂句混着用；有错误，但很少影响理解\\n- **口语四项**：\\n  - 流利和连贯（Fluency and Coherence）：愿意说长，偶尔重复、自我纠正或停顿都可以，但不能一直卡\\n  - 词汇（Lexical Resource）：话题词够用，词不会时能换个说法解释（paraphrase）\\n  - 语法（Grammatical Range and Accuracy）：简单句和复杂句都有，复杂句常出错但不太影响理解\\n  - 发音（Pronunciation）：大体能听懂，有些词发音不清没关系\\n- **最重要的一点**：6 分不要求没错误，要求的是\\"说得长、写得完整、意思清楚\\"。练习时先保证完成任务和连贯，再追求高级词"}]`),y=f,w=s=>y.filter(e=>e.chapter===s),u=s=>s.replace(/[&<>"]/g,e=>({"&":"&amp;","<":"&lt;",">":"&gt;",'"':"&quot;"})[e]),d=s=>u(s).replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g,"<b>$1</b>").replace(/`([^`]+)`/g,"<code>$1</code>").replace(/\[([^\]]+)\]\((https?:[^)]+)\)/g,'<a href="$2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">$1</a>').replace(new RegExp(`(?<!["'>])(https?:\\/\\/[^\\s<，。；）)]+)`,"g"),'<a href="$1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">$1</a>');function g(s){const e=s.split(`
`),h=[];let t=0;for(;t<e.length;){const r=e[t];if(!r.trim()){t++;continue}if(r.startsWith("```")){const a=[];for(t++;t<e.length&&!e[t].startsWith("```");)a.push(e[t++]);t++,h.push(`<pre class="essay en">${u(a.join(`
`))}</pre>`);continue}const i=r.match(/^(#{4,6}) (.+)$/);if(i){h.push(`<h3>${d(i[2])}</h3>`),t++;continue}if(r.startsWith("|")){const a=[];for(;t<e.length&&e[t].startsWith("|");)/^\|\s*:?-/.test(e[t])||a.push(e[t].trim().replace(/^\||\|$/g,"").split("|").map(n=>n.trim())),t++;const[l,...o]=a;h.push(`<div class="tbl"><table><thead><tr>${l.map(n=>`<th>${d(n)}</th>`).join("")}</tr></thead><tbody>${o.map(n=>`<tr>${n.map(c=>`<td>${d(c)}</td>`).join("")}</tr>`).join("")}</tbody></table></div>`);continue}if(/^\s*([-*]|\d+\.)\s/.test(r)){const a=[];for(;t<e.length&&(/^\s*([-*]|\d+\.)\s/.test(e[t])||e[t].startsWith("    ")&&e[t].trim()&&a.length);){const n=e[t].match(/^(\s*)([-*]|\d+\.)\s+(.*)$/);n?a.push({indent:n[1].length,ordered:/\d/.test(n[2]),text:n[3]}):a[a.length-1].text+=" "+e[t].trim(),t++}let l="";const o=[];for(const n of a){for(;o.length&&n.indent<o[o.length-1].indent;)l+=`</li></${o.pop().tag}>`;const c=o[o.length-1];if(!c||n.indent>c.indent){const p=n.ordered?"ol":"ul";o.push({indent:n.indent,tag:p}),l+=`<${p}><li>`}else l+="</li><li>";l+=d(n.text)}for(;o.length;)l+=`</li></${o.pop().tag}>`;h.push(l);continue}const m=[];for(;t<e.length&&e[t].trim()&&!/^(\s*([-*]|\d+\.)\s|\||```|#{4})/.test(e[t]);)m.push(e[t++]);h.push(`<p>${d(m.join(" "))}</p>`)}return h.join(`
`)}function b(s,e){const h=Array.isArray(e.chapter)?e.chapter:[e.chapter],t=y.filter(i=>h.includes(i.chapter)),r=t.find(i=>i.id===e.current)??t[0];s.innerHTML=`${e.extraTop??""}
    <div class="doc-wrap">
      <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="小节">${t.map(i=>`<a href="${e.base}/${i.id}" class="${i.id===r.id?"on":""}">${u(i.title.replace(/（.*?）$/,""))}</a>`).join("")}</nav>
      <article class="card doc-body"><h2 style="margin-top:0">${u(r.title)}</h2>${g(r.md)}</article>
    </div>`}export{y as a,b as d,w as s};
